{"markdown":{"yaml":{"pagetitle":"Data-Driven Modelling for Mechanical Systems","page-layout":"custom"},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n\n```{=html}\n<header class=\"topbar\">\n<div class=\"topbar-inner\">\n<a href=\"./index.html\" class=\"brand\">\n<div class=\"brand-mark\">ω</div>\n<div class=\"brand-meta\">\n<div class=\"brand-title\">Mechanical Systems Dynamics</div>\n<div class=\"brand-sub\">NMED 5XX / CS 401 · Interactive Tutorials Hub</div>\n</div>\n</a>\n<div class=\"topbar-actions\">\n<button id=\"theme-toggle-btn\" class=\"btn-nav\" aria-label=\"Toggle Light or Dark Theme\">\n<span>🌙 Dark</span>\n</button>\n</div>\n</div>\n</header>\n\n<section class=\"hero-band\">\n<div class=\"hero-inner\">\n<div class=\"eyebrow\">Graduate Mechanical Engineering · Fall Term 2026</div>\n<div class=\"copper-bar\"></div>\n<h1>Data-Driven Modelling for Mechanical Systems</h1>\n<p class=\"hero-lead\">\nA suite of interactive scientific computing tutorials connecting the theoretical foundations of \n<span class=\"highlight-blue\">vibrational mechanics</span>, \n<span class=\"highlight-orange\">spectral analysis</span>, and \n<span class=\"highlight-teal\">nonlinear dynamic systems</span> with live browser simulations, \ndiagnostic conceptual checkpoints, Beamer presentation slides, and runnable Python notebooks.\n</p>\n</div>\n</section>\n\n<main class=\"hub-wrap\">\n<div class=\"section-header\">\n<div class=\"section-tag\">Course Syllabus & Laboratory Modules</div>\n<h2>Available Interactive Tutorials</h2>\n<p>Select any lecture module below to explore rigorous theoretical formulations, manipulate real-time physical simulation parameters, and access source lecture materials.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"tutorial-grid\">\n\n<!-- Card 01 -->\n<article class=\"hub-card\">\n<div class=\"hub-card-body\">\n<div class=\"hub-card-kicker\">Lecture 01 · 1-DOF Dynamics</div>\n<h3 class=\"hub-card-title\">Why Does a Washing Machine Shake?</h3>\n<p class=\"hub-card-abstract\">Model a 1-DOF mass-spring-damper oscillator excited by rotating unbalance. Explore resonance, phase lag inversion, and passive self-isolation across spin speeds.</p>\n<div class=\"hub-card-tags\">\n<span class=\"hub-tag\">#ForcedVibration</span>\n<span class=\"hub-tag\">#Resonance</span>\n<span class=\"hub-tag\">#RotatingImbalance</span>\n<span class=\"hub-tag\">#Isolation</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"hub-card-footer\">\n<a href=\"./lectures/01-washing-machine-shake/index.html\" class=\"hub-card-link\">Open interactive tutorial ↗</a>\n<div class=\"hub-card-downloads\">\n<a href=\"./lectures/01-washing-machine-shake/slides.pdf\" download title=\"Download Slides PDF\">PDF</a> · \n<a href=\"./lectures/01-washing-machine-shake/notebook.ipynb\" download title=\"Download Notebook\">.ipynb</a>\n</div>\n</div>\n</article>\n\n<!-- Card 02 -->\n<article class=\"hub-card\">\n<div class=\"hub-card-body\">\n<div class=\"hub-card-kicker\">Lecture 02 · Signal Processing</div>\n<h3 class=\"hub-card-title\">Fourier Transform and FFT</h3>\n<p class=\"hub-card-abstract\">From continuous time series to discrete linear spectra. Master the DFT, O(N log N) Cooley-Tukey algorithm, the Nyquist-Shannon limit, and windowing functions.</p>\n<div class=\"hub-card-tags\">\n<span class=\"hub-tag\">#FFT</span>\n<span class=\"hub-tag\">#SpectralAnalysis</span>\n<span class=\"hub-tag\">#NyquistLimit</span>\n<span class=\"hub-tag\">#Windowing</span>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"hub-card-footer\">\n<a href=\"./lectures/02-fourier-transform-fft/index.html\" class=\"hub-card-link\">Open interactive tutorial ↗</a>\n<div class=\"hub-card-downloads\">\n<a href=\"./lectures/02-fourier-transform-fft/slides.pdf\" download title=\"Download Slides PDF\">PDF</a> · \n<a href=\"./lectures/02-fourier-transform-fft/notebook.ipynb\" download title=\"Download Notebook\">.ipynb</a>\n</div>\n</div>\n</article>\n\n<!-- Card 03 -->\n<article class=\"hub-card\">\n<div class=\"hub-card-body\">\n<div class=\"hub-card-kicker\